# Copy to .env and fill in. NEVER commit .env.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
KAULI_PIPER_VOICE=./data/voices/en_GB-alba-medium.onnx

# Signs the login session cookie - required before deploying anywhere
# reachable from the internet. Generate with:
#   python3 -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
KAULI_SESSION_SECRET=

# FinOps guard on the ops dashboard - flags today's real Claude MT spend
# once it crosses this many dollars. Defaults to 5.0 if unset; raise it
# once real usage tells you what a normal day actually costs.
# KAULI_DAILY_AI_COST_ALERT_USD=5.0

# --tts xtts (voice cloning) - optional override; pipeline.py auto-extracts
# a reference clip from the source audio if this is left blank. ONLY point
# this at audio you have the speaker's consent to clone.
# Also needs COQUI_TOS_AGREED=1 set for non-interactive runs (CPML license).
# KAULI_XTTS_REFERENCE=

# Real auth (replaces webapp's mocked login) - email/password + Google via
# Supabase Auth. From Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API.
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Google sign-in needs no extra keys here - it's configured on Supabase's
# side (Authentication -> Providers -> Google) once you've set up the
# Google Cloud OAuth client per the setup steps.
# KAULI_STAFF_EMAILS=you@example.com   # comma-separated, gets 'staff' role
# KAULI_TEST_CLIENT_EMAILS=you@example.com   # comma-separated, full access on every plan, for testing

# --- billing (webapp/billing.py) ---
# Paystack: dashboard.paystack.com -> Settings -> API Keys & Webhooks.
# Two separate slots, not one - PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY (test) is always what
# routine development/testing uses; PAYSTACK_LIVE_SECRET_KEY only gets
# used at all when PAYSTACK_LIVE_MODE=true is set explicitly. Going live
# is then a deliberate, reversible flip of one flag, not just "whichever
# key happens to be pasted in." Also set the webhook URL in the Paystack
# dashboard to <your-deployed-url>/webhooks/paystack (can't point at
# localhost - Paystack needs a publicly reachable URL).
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=
# PAYSTACK_LIVE_SECRET_KEY=
# PAYSTACK_LIVE_MODE=false

# M-Pesa (Safaricom Daraja API): developer.safaricom.co.ke -> create an app
# for sandbox credentials (free, instant). Production needs a real
# registered paybill and Safaricom's approval - that's a real business
# process, not a config change. MPESA_ENV=sandbox|production.
# MPESA_CONSUMER_KEY=
# MPESA_CONSUMER_SECRET=
# MPESA_SHORTCODE=
# MPESA_PASSKEY=
# MPESA_ENV=sandbox
# NOTE: Safaricom's callback needs a PUBLICLY reachable URL - it cannot
# call back to localhost. Testing the actual STK-push round trip needs
# either a real deployment or a tunnel (ngrok etc.) pointed at this
# machine while you test.

# USD->KES conversion falls back to this if the free live-rate API is down.
# KAULI_USD_KES_FALLBACK_RATE=129.0

# --- marketing site ("/" for logged-out visitors, webapp/templates/marketing.html) ---
# Paste your Calendly scheduling link (calendly.com -> Event Types -> your
# event -> Share -> "Add to Website" -> the plain event URL, e.g.
# https://calendly.com/your-name/consultation) to embed a live booking
# widget on the "Book a call" section. Leave unset and the page just shows
# phone/email + the "Request a callback" form (fully working either way).
# KAULI_CALENDLY_URL=

# Optional - cross-posts a blog post to DEV.to (with a canonical_url back
# to the real Kauli post) when staff click "Publish to DEV.to" on
# /staff/blog. Free, no waitlist: generate a real key from your OWN
# DEV.to account: Settings -> Extensions -> DEV API Keys. Leave unset and
# that button just doesn't appear - webapp/devto_publish.py.
# DEV_TO_API_KEY=

# Optional - same idea, on Medium. Generate a real token from your OWN
# Medium account: Settings -> Security and apps -> Integration tokens.
# As of when this was written, Medium's self-service token page wasn't
# reachable, so DEV.to above is the reliable free option right now - this
# is here for whenever/if that changes. webapp/medium_publish.py.
# MEDIUM_INTEGRATION_TOKEN=

# Optional - powers the "YouTube auto-import" section on the client
# dashboard: periodically checks a client's channel/playlist for new
# PUBLIC videos (read-only, no OAuth) and surfaces them to turn into a
# real order with one click - never auto-creates or bills an order itself.
# Get a free key from Google Cloud Console: create/select a project ->
# APIs & Services -> enable "YouTube Data API v3" -> Credentials -> Create
# API key. No app review needed for this read-only key (that's only
# required for OAuth write-scopes, which this doesn't use). Leave unset
# and the section just explains it's not set up yet.
# webapp/youtube_poll.py.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Real outbound email via Brevo (webapp/mailer.py) - powers auto-sent
# receipts (see app.py's _activate_payment). In Brevo: Settings -> SMTP &
# API -> API Keys -> generate a new API key (paste it here, never in chat
# or a commit); Settings -> Senders, Domains & Dedicated IPs -> add and
# verify the address you're sending from (BREVO_FROM_EMAIL must match a
# verified sender or Brevo rejects the send). New Brevo accounts also need
# a verified phone number on the account itself before ANY send goes out -
# a one-time step in Brevo's own UI, not something this app can do for
# you. Leave these unset and receipts still get created and are viewable
# any time, they just wait in "Receipts awaiting delivery" on
# /staff/billing for a staff member to forward them manually.
# BREVO_API_KEY=
# BREVO_FROM_EMAIL=receipts@yourdomain.com

# Only when you move to cloud
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=eu-west-1
# KAULI_S3_BUCKET=
# AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=
# AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=
